<title>BELGIUM: Sabena HQ evacuated after bomb alert.</title>
<headline>Sabena HQ evacuated after bomb alert.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The headquarters of Belgian national airline Sabena were evacuated on Wednesday after a bomb alert, police said.</p>
<p>The warning said the alleged device was due to explode at 1800 local (1600 GMT), but by 1810 local there was still no sign of an explosion.</p>
<p>A police official said the nearby airport terminal was not evacuated and that plane traffic suffered no delays.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
